cial, Inc. was founded in 1871 and is headquartered in Glen Allen, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas Joseph McInerney | President, CEO & Director | Age 68 | Compensation: $4.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $2.4M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $19K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Genworth Financial Inc is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.2B market cap on $7.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 2.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 7.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 24% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Valued at a 31% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Genworth (GNW) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/genworth-gnw-q3-2026-earnings-184408000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793904519.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Genworth targets $275M-$300M in 2026 share repurchases as CEO transition to CFO Upton is set for year-end (NYSE:GNW)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4666997-genworth-targets-275m-300m-in-2026-share-repurchases-as-ceo-transition-to-cfo-upton-is-set","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793900887.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership","dividend"]},{"title":"Genworth Financial (NYSE:GNW) Releases Quarterly Earnings Results, Misses Estimates By $0.01 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"ht